			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodule — breaker skips failure count when Open\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to e799e065, integrating a Cocoon circuit breaker fix that prevents in-flight gRPC completions from accumulating failure counts after the breaker has already tripped Open.\n\nCocoon's CheckCircuitBreaker was incrementing the failure counter unconditionally on every error completion, even when the breaker state was already Open. In-flight requests arriving after the trip could push the counter well beyond the intended threshold (observed at N≥19) and produce noisy \"transition from=OPEN to=Open failures=N\" debug-log lines on every additional error.\n\nThe fix returns early when the state is Open, logging the post-trip completion at debug level without counting it. Recovery remains driven by the existing timeout-based transition to HalfOpen, unchanged.\n\nThis eliminates dev-log chatter and keeps the failure counter accurate within the Closed and HalfOpen observation windows that actually drive breaker state transitions.",
			"SHA": "3a783a02027449085b4eb76da4d7c269c7862b31"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T20:55:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodule — circuit breaker tolerates unknown gRPC methods\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to 119b4c70, integrating a Cocoon fix for false circuit breaker trips caused by unknown-method probe responses.\n\nCocoon's GRPCServerService dispatcher was counting unrecognized gRPC method names as failure events in the circuit breaker health counter. When Mountain probes for methods routed to subsystems outside Cocoon's handler registry, or when method sets evolve independently across the gRPC boundary, these expected unknown-method responses could trip the circuit breaker open, disrupting legitimate extension host requests.\n\nThe fix filters unknown-method errors from the circuit breaker's failure accounting while still returning a proper error response to the caller. Only genuine transport or handler errors now trigger breaker state transitions, ensuring stable operation during cross-subsystem method probes and asymmetric method set evolution.",
			"SHA": "8bcc9f55bf3de0b17590061062b70b95ad42f43c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T20:47:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodule — storage RPC fix, clean identifiers, per-subsystem tier routing\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to cdef6cce, integrating fixes across Cocoon, Mountain, Output, and Wind submodules.\n\nCocoon corrects the RPC method name in the storage cache priming path from `storage:getItems` (kebab-case, object arg) to `Storage.GetItems` (PascalCase, empty array), matching Mountain's RPC dispatcher contract. Without this fix, extensions reading workspace or global state synchronously during `activate()` — Roo Code, Copilot, GitLens — received only defaults after every reload, causing UI state regressions across session boundaries.\n\nMountain restores \"Mountain\" as the crate binary, library, and package name, and the Tauri productName and bundle identifier, replacing the verbose development build descriptors introduced in the prior commit. The Cocoon sidecar launch is now gated on both `ExtensionHostCocoon` feature and absence of `no_node_host` cfg so the Node-vs-WebWorker tier is respected at boot. Includes task type in task provider Options payload for correct Cocoon task registration, derives Clone on ExtensionCollection for shared terminal env mutation, and adds zsh shell integration script to the Tauri resource bundle.\n\nOutput introduces per-subsystem tier resolution in the TauriChannel IPC router, enabling channels to route to Mountain or Cocoon independently rather than being governed by a single global `_TierIPC` variable. Routes `tasks` and `auth` to Node by default while keeping most subsystems on Mountain.\n\nWind wires the runtime dispatch layer in TauriMainProcessService that reads per-subsystem tier overrides from env vars and `__LandTiers` globals, routing channels resolved to \"Node\" directly to Cocoon via the `cocoon:request` bridge.\n\nExtension storage now persists correctly across reloads, development builds use clean identifiers, and the IPC tier routing supports per-subsystem dispatch across the Mountain-Cocoon boundary, completing TIER-SYSTEM Step 4b.",
			"SHA": "c9b02f8863a7fcd422e399726413cd573f02ddd3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:33:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodule — dev build isolation, module resolution, dependency fixes\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to ad1d49c2, integrating downstream fixes across six component submodules.\n\nMountain renames its crate binary, library, Tauri productName, and bundle identifier to a verbose development build descriptor (Node 22, VS Code dependency, debug profile, esbuild compiler), preventing binary name and macOS Bundle ID collisions with the release build. The Tauri resource bundle expands to include all Sky deployment variant directories.\n\nSky replaces three bare `@codeeditorland/sky` package specifiers in workbench entry points with explicit relative paths to `Function/Sky/Bridge.js`, ensuring deterministic module resolution when the build pipeline does not alias the package name to the Sky source directory.\n\nOutput adds the missing `browserslist` dependency to its package manifest, resolving an unhandled peer dependency that could cause downstream build failures.\n\nCocoon regenerates compiled JavaScript output, folding several target files into a single consolidated bootstrap pipeline through `Target/Effect/RPCServer.js`.\n\nMaintain relocates the `IsFreeVarSafe` check and `FindSubstSite` resolution from the eliminator loop into `TryBlockPreserve` in mod.rs, where the Preserve-pass text-patching logic actually consumes them.\n\nWind regenerates its TypeScript incremental build metadata for updated program structure after the module resolution changes.\n\nDevelopment and release builds now install side-by-side without Bundle ID conflicts, all entry points resolve the Sky bridge deterministically, and the missing browserslist dependency is restored.",
			"SHA": "e6bbbe61ebb7a6a77013e1275099c329357d9251"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:13:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance Element submodules — extension env collections, decoration rendering, tier routing expansion\n\nAdvance the Element and Dependency submodule pointers to integrate upstream VS Code improvements and close systemic gaps across the extension-host API surface, decoration pipeline, and IPC routing infrastructure.\n\n**Element (c7f7c6da):**\n- Cocoon replaces a dozen no-op stubs with real implementations — EnvironmentVariableCollection mutations forward to Mountain via terminal.envCollection.* notifications; workspaceState/globalState caches prime before activate(); extensionUri uses MakeUri(); registerTextEditorCommand drives atomic TextEditorEdit edits; language provider metadata flows to Mountain for correct Monaco invocation; executeTask returns a real handle; LogOutputChannel provides ISO-8601 timestamped, level-filtered output; status bar items support 1.74+ overloads with idempotent disposal; webview panels gain live viewColumn/active/visible tracking; tree data providers subscribe onDidChangeTreeData; filesystem writes encode binary as Uint8Array; applyEdit returns Mountain's actual success boolean. Adds __LandTier_* esbuild defines for 15 subsystems.\n- Mountain implements TerminalEnvCollection — a global registry dispatching Replace/Append/Prepend/Delete/Clear/SetPersistent/SetDescription from seven Vine terminal.envCollection.* handlers, applying registered mutators at every PTY spawn. Adds tree.refresh and outputChannel.replace Vine notification relays. Expands tier routing defaults to 14 additional subsystems; extends LandFixTier::LogResolvedTiers to emit all 16 values at boot.\n- Output exposes ICodeEditorService on the CELExposeAccessor services facade so extension decoration APIs paint visible squiggles, gutter icons, and inline hints.\n- Sky registers decoration types with ICodeEditorService in InstallTasksAndDecorations, switches to setDecorationsByType, wires panel-mode webview lifecycle with postMessage/dispose/viewState forwarding, adds sky://output/replace and sky://tree-view/refresh handlers.\n- Wind adds 14 per-subsystem IPC routing tier definitions with union types and default profiles.\n- Worker adds deepmerge-ts 7.1.5 for type-safe recursive ESBuild config merging.\n- Rest normalises shell redirection spacing and case indentation across scripts.\n\n**Dependency (e481e786):**\n- Advance Microsoft VS Code Editor submodule pointer for upstream changeset lifecycle caching and eviction, offline BYOK state resilience with proper reconnection reconciliation, and a dedicated sessions link in the chat view.\n\nExtension environment variables now survive reload, decorations paint on first render, webview panels remain interactive, output channels update atomically, tree views respond to data changes, and the IPC tier routing layer covers all 16 subsystems across Mountain ↔ Cocoon ↔ Wind ↔ Sky.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "35267970979a025481d75b3a82b4b2e223a89de5"
		}
	],
